Bugfix: Report errors when closing restored files in `restore`

Since restic 0.19.0, `restore` ignored errors that occurred when closing a
restored file. Some filesystems, for example NFS or filesystems with quotas,
only report write errors when a file is closed. In this case `restore` could
finish successfully although files were incomplete. Restic now reports such
errors for the affected file and exits with an error.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22179
